############ HOW TO READ IT ############
  [CUDA memcpy HtoD] on the host arm should be ~= the logical dataset
  size. On the device arm it should be ~0 for the input. That delta is
  the overhead a filter cannot avoid, because H5Z only ever sees host
  bytes.

  If BOTH arms show the same HtoD, BENCH_DEVICE_INPUT is not wired up
  and the run proves nothing -- fix the benchmark, not the plot.

